        answer: "បាទ **Quick Mask Mode (ចុចអក្សរ Q) គឺជាវិធីជ្រើសរើសវត្ថុ (Selection) ដោយប្រើជក់លាបពណ៌ក្រហម!**\n\nពេលខ្លះបន្ទាត់អង្រ្កង (Marching Ants) ធ្វើឱ្យវិលមុខ ហើយរើសកន្លែងតូចៗពិបាក។\n១. គ្រាន់តែចុចអក្សរ **Q** លើ Keyboard។\n២. រូបភាពទាំងមូលនឹងត្រូវគ្របដណ្ដប់ដោយពណ៌ក្រហមថ្លាៗ (Ruby Overlay)។\n៣. យកជក់ (Paint Brush) ពណ៌ស លាបលើកន្លែងណាដែលអ្នកចង់ Select (ពណ៌ក្រហមនឹងរលាយបាត់)។ ឬលាបពណ៌ខ្មៅ ដើម្បីដកការ Select នោះចេញវិញ។\n៤. ពេលអ្នកផាត់រាងរួចរាល់ ចុចអក្សរ **Q** ម្តងទៀត។ ផ្ទៃដែលអ្នកលាបពណ៌សអម្បាញ់មិញ នឹងប្រែទៅជាបន្ទាត់អង្រ្កង Selection យ៉ាងស្អាតឥតខ្ចោះ!\n\n💡 វិធីនេះល្អខ្លាំងសម្រាប់ការរើសផ្នែកណាមួយឱ្យព្រិលៗ (Soft Selection) ដោយប្រើជក់ក្បាលព្រិល (Soft Brush)។",
        answer_en: "**Quick Mask Mode (Shortcut: Q) transforms rigid 'marching ants' selections into a fluid, brushable ruby overlay!**\n\nSometimes manipulating selection boxes and lassos is frustratingly rigid.\n1. Simply press **Q** on your keyboard.\n2. Your entire canvas is immediately bathed in a semi-transparent Ruby Red overlay.\n3. Switch to a standard Paint Brush. Painting with pure White erases the red overlay (creating a selection), while painting with pure Black restores the red overlay (removing from the selection).\n4. Once your silhouette is flawlessly painted, press **Q** again. The red overlay vanishes, instantly converting into a live, perfect marching-ants selection boundary!\n\n💡 **The Ultimate Advantage:** Because you are painting the selection, you can use a large Soft Brush. This creates mathematical Alpha transparency selections, allowing you to gradually feather effects into an image rather than having hard cut-off lines.",
        chips: ["Advanced Mask Manipulation", "Erase Brush vs Masking"],
        chips_en: ["Advanced Masking (Grayscale)", "Erase Brush vs Masking"]
