        answer_en: "**If your photo is severely underexposed (too dark) or you shot a subject backlit against the sun, this is your immediate rescue tool!**\n\nDeploy a **Shadows / Highlights Adjustment Layer** from the Layers panel:\n- **Shadows Slider:** Dragging this to the right aggressively targets the darkest pixels in the image (like a silhouette) and artificially illuminates them, revealing hidden facial details and textures without blowing out the rest of the image.\n- **Highlights Slider:** Dragging this to the left targets blindingly bright pixels (like a blown-out white sky) and aggressively darkens them, attempting to recover lost cloud details.\n\n💡 It's the fastest way to balance a poorly exposed JPG, though processing a RAW file in the Develop Persona yields exponentially better recovery.",
